  "description": "Erection of a single storey side extension to the house and installation of a replacement front boundary vehicular gate and pedestrian gate.  ",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications:  SCR A110 A, SCR A111 A, SCR A115 A, SCR A120 A\r\nReceived: 18 June 2026,  SCR A122 C, SCR A125 B Received: 11 June 2026,  SCR A05 A Received: 21 April 2026,  SCR A10 A, SCR A11 A, SCR A15 A, SCR A20 A, SCR A21 A, PP-14827249v1 Received: 02 April 2026.  \r\n\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the appearance of the area.",
    "Condition : 4 - The replacement front boundary wall and pillars hereby permitted shall be constructed with red brick and replacement front boundary pedestrian and vehicular gates hereby permitted shall be painted close board and railing timber gates only.  \r\n\r\nReasons:  To protect the character and appearance of the site, streetscene and Chiswick House Conservation Area.  ",
    "Condition : 5 - No additional windows or openings shall be formed in the front, side and rear elevations, or roof, of the development hereby permitted.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to protect neighbours' privacy.\r\n"
  ],
